WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.890
In 2010, the world's food supply came to
2,825 kilocalories per person per day.

2
00:00:07.940 --> 00:00:12.290
By 2023, it had risen to 3,016.

3
00:00:12.340 --> 00:00:17.740
Yet in 2025, around 645 million
people were undernourished:

4
00:00:17.790 --> 00:00:21.670
7.8 per cent of the world's population.

5
00:00:21.720 --> 00:00:25.490
So if the food is there,
why are so many hungry?

6
00:00:25.540 --> 00:00:26.830
Are the figures wrong?

7
00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:28.950
Is it all shipped to rich countries?

8
00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:32.750
In this mission, you'll learn
how geographers measure hunger,

9
00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:36.290
from undernourishment to
child stunting and wasting.

10
00:00:36.340 --> 00:00:39.350
Then you'll map the 2026
Global Hunger Index,

11
00:00:39.400 --> 00:00:43.070
and ask who funds the indices you rely on.

12
00:00:43.120 --> 00:00:48.530
Your mission: explain how about 3,000
calories per person can exist alongside

13
00:00:48.580 --> 00:00:52.110
around 645 million hungry people.
